# PostDelegate

PostDelegate is a social media scheduler. Use its MCP server for interactive work and its REST API from code. Latest version of this rule: {{site}}/agents/postdelegate.mdc. Full agent guide: {{site}}/agents/AGENTS.md.

## Connect

{{connect}}

Cursor MCP config (`.cursor/mcp.json`):

```json
{ "mcpServers": { "postdelegate": { "url": "{{mcp_oauth}}" } } }
```

## Workflow

1. List channels: MCP `integrationList` / REST `GET /integrations` (REST also returns `disabled`; skip channels with `disabled: true`, they are paused).
2. Read the network's rules and settings: MCP `integrationSchema` (`platform`, `isPremium: false`) / REST `GET /integration-settings/:id`. Look up ids with MCP `triggerTool` / REST `POST /integration-trigger/:id`.
3. Upload media first: MCP `uploadFromUrlTool` / REST `POST /upload` or `POST /upload-from-url`. With `adjust`, wait for `ready` (MCP `mediaStatusTool` / REST `GET /media/:id/status`).
4. Create a **draft**: MCP `integrationSchedulePostTool` (`settings` is a `[{key, value}]` list) / REST `POST /posts` (`settings` is an object, `{}` when none; `shortLink` and `tags` required; one `date` per request).
5. List, change or delete: MCP `postsListTool`, `postSettingsTool`, `deletePostTool` / REST `GET /posts`, `PUT /posts/:id/settings`, `DELETE /posts/:id`.

6. Studio video: MCP `studioTemplatesTool` → `studioRenderTool` → `studioRenderStatusTool` / REST `GET /studio/templates` → `POST /studio/renders` `{ template, spec, name? }` → poll `GET /studio/renders/:id`. Follow the template's `schema`, media are `mediaId`s from the media library (never URLs). On `completed`, post the returned `path` as a draft with step 4. Rendering never posts. Templates (`identifier`): `hook-over-clip`, `talking-head-captions`, `image-slideshow`, `before-after`, `top-n-list`, `quote-card` and `ai-ugc`. For `ai-ugc`, write `script` (`hook`, `lines`, `cta`) yourself and leave `voiceover` at its default `false`: it renders with no AI key. `voiceover: true` and `stills` need the workspace's own OpenAI key. `music.assetId` must be a music already uploaded in Studio.

Content is HTML: each line in `<p>`. Dates are UTC ISO 8601. REST `POST /posts` is limited to 30 requests per workspace per hour, so batch channels that share a date into one request.

